    "note": [
     {
      "text": "71-year-old female presenting with excessive thirst and frequent urination for 4 months. Character: passing urine many times, also at night; radiation: n/a; aggravated by sweet food; relieved by nothing. Severity 2/10. Associated: blurred vision. PMH: Type 2 diabetes for 15 years; Hypertension for 10 years. Drugs: Metformin 500 mg; Amlodipine 5 mg. Allergy: penicillin. Family: hypertension. Personal: non-smoker, no alcohol. Triage: ROUTINE."
